course: dictionary
lesson: 7985
title: Recover: getting well, getting back, feeling normal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To recover means to get well again after an illness or injury. It can also mean to get back something that was lost or stolen, or to feel normal again after a shock. The words around recover show you which meaning is right.
explain: «A hedgehog in a garden in Kent was tangled in a loose football net overnight.» It was found weak and cut, and it «needed weeks at a rescue to recover». Weak and cut tell you it was hurt, so recover means to get well again.
explain: Recovery is the noun, the act of getting better or getting back. Recovered and recovering are the past and the -ing forms. «Humpbacks have recovered a lot» since most whaling was banned, which means their numbers have grown again.
fact: Recover means to get well again after an illness or injury.
fact: Recover can also mean to get back something that was lost or stolen.
fact: To recover from a shock means to feel normal again.
fact: «Whaling», the hunting of whales for oil and meat, nearly wiped out some species, and most whaling was banned in 1986.
fact: Useful phrases: recover from, fully recover, recover quickly, make a full recovery.
exercise: «A hedgehog was tangled in a loose football net overnight.» In the morning it needed weeks at a rescue to recover. What does recover mean here? | Get lost in the garden | Fall asleep for good | *Get well again | Play football all day
exercise: A team that has a bad start in a match can recover. What does recover mean in sport? | Give up the match | *Get back into a good position | Run off the field | Get hurt on the pitch
exercise: Which word is the noun for getting better? | recover | *recovery | recovering | recovers
test: A thief took Mia's bike, but the police managed to recover it. What does recover mean? | Lend it to a friend | *Get back something that was stolen | Break it into pieces | Sell it to a shop
test: After a scary fall, Sam needed a few minutes to recover from the shock. What does recover mean here? | Fall over again | Forget his own name | *Feel normal again | Start running fast
exam: «Ella's team were losing badly at half time, but they recovered to win the match.» What does recovered mean? | Went home early | Stopped playing for the day | *Got back into a good position | Lost their kit
